    <p class="eyebrow">A native Mac file manager for people with servers</p>
    <h1>Two panes over ssh. <span class="serif">Your tools underneath.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">pālana points either pane at any host in your
    <code>~/.ssh/config</code>—or at your Mac—and drives the tools the
    servers already have. Browse, copy, and move with vim keys. A real shell
    on the focused host sits under the panes; <kbd>⌘`</kbd> hands it the
    keyboard and hands it back. Every command pālana composes is on screen
    before it runs, and every one of them pastes into a terminal. Where a
    host runs ZFS, datasets, snapshots, and send/receive are one key
    away.</p>
    <p class="hero-tagline">Terminal tools. A readable interface.</p>
