<div class="sec-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">The field</p>
  <h2>Every host, its pools, and when you last looked.</h2>
</div>

<div class="frow rev">
  <div class="frow-text">
    <p>Press <kbd>f</kbd> for your hosts, their pools and datasets, what
    each can do—<code>zfs</code>, <code>rsync</code>, sudo—and the date
    each was last probed. <kbd>r</kbd> probes a host again in place.
    <kbd>⏎</kbd> points a pane at it. <kbd>F</kbd> opens the full map,
    every mount on every machine, for a second display. pālana records what
    it found and when; it refreshes only when you ask.
    <a href="/field/">See the field →</a></p>
  </div>
